    },
    "message": "Read the indexing process's pipe on its own thread so a save does not wait for the ingest in progress\n\nA save's message is larger than the pipe's buffer, so its send blocked until the\nindexing process finished the ingest before it: about 25.8 s of a seven-day run.\nThe benchmark now times the parts of a save outside capture and the store's write.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
