    },
    "message": "Encode each world field once in a capture and read the restore check's records from their bytes\n\nThe hash tree encoded the JSON the document was parsed from again; each field now\nkeeps its bytes for the document, its hash and its archive chunks. The restore check\nshows the live records are exactly what their saved bytes restore without building\nthem, and compares restored records for anything it can not show exactly. Adds the\nindex_row kernel the next commits use.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
