    },
    "message": "Compress a save's chunks on a few threads and drop repeated work in saves and frames\n\nThe save still waits for the threads and writes on its own thread; the bytes are the\nsame. A frame encodes in Rust and no longer copies what its final dump copies, and a\nnew chunk asks for a v1/v2 chunk file only where such a directory exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
