    },
    "message": "Make the indexing process cheap enough not to hold the computation back\n\nThe index was the limit of a long computation: 168 s of CPU over 336 saves. A new\nindex no longer has entity_time, which no query reads, and entity_turn_order holds\nonly conversations, so a commit journals and writes far fewer random pages. The\nindexing process keeps one connection and a larger cache between saves, a current\nfile is not written just to open it, rows are read in one pass in Rust, and the\nprivacy check's key cache holds every relationship key of a save.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
